WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.334 --> 00:00:03.603
-My first guest tonight
is a hip-hop legend

00:00:03.603 --> 00:00:06.105
and one of the biggest
entertainers in the world.

00:00:06.105 --> 00:00:08.741
You can see him
in the new show "BMF,"

00:00:08.741 --> 00:00:11.811
which airs Sundays at 8:00 p.m.
on Starz,

00:00:11.811 --> 00:00:14.213
and he lends his voice
to the new animated movie

00:00:14.213 --> 00:00:17.383
"The Addams Family 2,"
which is in theaters on Friday.

00:00:17.383 --> 00:00:20.620
Here is Snoop Dogg, everybody.

00:00:20.620 --> 00:00:23.489
That's what I'm talking about,
yeah.

00:00:23.489 --> 00:00:25.692
That's exactly
what I'm talking about.

00:00:25.692 --> 00:00:27.860
You look good, buddy.
Welcome.

00:00:27.860 --> 00:00:29.495
-What's up, Jimmy?
What's happening?

00:00:29.495 --> 00:00:31.865
-I'm so happy
you came back to the show.

00:00:31.865 --> 00:00:33.966
Happy almost 50th birthday?

00:00:33.966 --> 00:00:35.735
Are you turning 50?

00:00:35.735 --> 00:00:37.970
-Yeah, I'm about to be 5-0, man.

00:00:37.970 --> 00:00:39.839
-Wow, you're about to be 5-0.

00:00:39.839 --> 00:00:42.041
And doing anything special
for the birthday?

00:00:42.041 --> 00:00:43.209
I'm assuming.

00:00:43.209 --> 00:00:45.111
-Yeah, my wife
is throwing a party for me,

00:00:45.111 --> 00:00:47.346
a players ball
for my 50th birthday party,

00:00:47.346 --> 00:00:50.783
so, you know, we're gonna be
suited in booty,

00:00:50.783 --> 00:00:52.852
You know what I'm saying?
Ready to do what we do.

00:00:52.852 --> 00:00:55.321
-Yeah.
That's -- And how --

00:00:55.321 --> 00:00:58.524
I wanted to ask you this
question because I never have.

00:00:58.524 --> 00:01:00.392
I think when people
hang out with you,

00:01:00.392 --> 00:01:02.762
they think that they
should smoke weed with you

00:01:02.762 --> 00:01:05.498
or try to smoke or keep up
with you, I think.

00:01:05.498 --> 00:01:06.799
Is that true?

00:01:06.799 --> 00:01:08.434
Do people just go up to you
and go, "Let's go for it?

00:01:08.434 --> 00:01:11.838
Let's see if I can keep up
with Snoop Dogg?"

00:01:11.838 --> 00:01:14.340
-I mean, I filled a lot
of hospital beds

00:01:14.340 --> 00:01:16.543
with those kind of people,
Jimmy.

00:01:16.543 --> 00:01:19.044
Like, this is a grown-man sport.

00:01:19.044 --> 00:01:20.746
I'm a heavyweight, so --
-I know.

00:01:20.746 --> 00:01:23.116
That's exactly right.
-When you step in the ring,

00:01:23.116 --> 00:01:24.684
you got to be prepared
for all things,

00:01:24.684 --> 00:01:26.352
and, I mean, a lot of times
people want to do it,

00:01:26.352 --> 00:01:27.686
but until they get in the ring

00:01:27.686 --> 00:01:29.622
and they really understand
what they're getting into.

00:01:29.622 --> 00:01:32.425
-Yeah, I would never
even go near the ring.

00:01:32.425 --> 00:01:34.661
I would -- Yeah.
I know you too well.

00:01:34.661 --> 00:01:38.197
I wouldn't even remotely go near
that, but I know -- I heard --

00:01:38.197 --> 00:01:40.700
-You know when I come down
to your show in real life,

00:01:40.700 --> 00:01:42.535
when I'm really there,
I blow the room out,

00:01:42.535 --> 00:01:44.470
you be trying to move me
to different floors

00:01:44.470 --> 00:01:46.773
and move me far away from y'all.

00:01:46.773 --> 00:01:48.641
[ Cheers and applause ]

00:01:48.641 --> 00:01:51.978
-[ Laughs ]

00:01:51.978 --> 00:01:53.680
That is exactly --

00:01:53.680 --> 00:01:56.849
That is so true
that I can't believe it.

00:01:56.849 --> 00:01:59.719
We actually try to have you
on a different floor

00:01:59.719 --> 00:02:02.055
because everyone has to
work here, you know?

00:02:02.055 --> 00:02:05.491
I get worried.
I get worried about --

00:02:05.491 --> 00:02:07.927
I want to talk to you about --

00:02:07.927 --> 00:02:12.297
You just joined Def Jam
as an executive creative

00:02:12.297 --> 00:02:14.366
and strategic consultant.

00:02:14.366 --> 00:02:16.169
Snoop Dogg at Def Jam.

00:02:16.169 --> 00:02:21.273
I love this idea, but how
and why did you want this?

00:02:21.273 --> 00:02:24.177
-Well, I was a fan
of Def Jam Records as a kid,

00:02:24.177 --> 00:02:26.646
and, you know, knowing
the talent they have over there

00:02:26.646 --> 00:02:28.547
and the opportunity
that was waiting on me,

00:02:28.547 --> 00:02:30.350
I wanted to go over there
and give a lot of opportunity

00:02:30.350 --> 00:02:32.584
to the artists over there to get
some information, some wisdom,

00:02:32.584 --> 00:02:34.053
and some guidance from me

00:02:34.053 --> 00:02:35.588
and then also develop
some new acts

00:02:35.588 --> 00:02:36.755
and give some opportunities,

00:02:36.755 --> 00:02:39.158
so Def Jam was the perfect place
for me

00:02:39.158 --> 00:02:41.894
considering how much I love it
and how much it means to hip-hop

00:02:41.894 --> 00:02:43.997
and how it really needed
somebody like me

00:02:43.997 --> 00:02:45.498
to come and change the energy
of the building.

00:02:45.498 --> 00:02:47.500
So I'm over there
for one reason --

00:02:47.500 --> 00:02:49.368
to get the music back popping

00:02:49.368 --> 00:02:51.804
and to make people feel
like they're supposed to feel.

00:02:51.804 --> 00:02:53.839
-I love that you're at Def Jam.

00:02:53.839 --> 00:02:55.041
I love Def Jam.

00:02:55.041 --> 00:02:58.411
Such an important part of music.

00:02:58.411 --> 00:03:04.850
Does that maybe hint at, maybe,
a new Snoop Dogg album? No?

00:03:04.850 --> 00:03:06.019
-Yeah, we got an album
coming out.

00:03:06.019 --> 00:03:08.187
It's called "Algorithm."
It'll be out in November.

00:03:08.187 --> 00:03:10.723
And it's featuring a lot of
big-name acts and some new ones.

00:03:10.723 --> 00:03:11.858
Yes, sir.

00:03:11.858 --> 00:03:13.226
-Whoa.

00:03:13.226 --> 00:03:14.993
That was more info than
I thought I was going to get.

00:03:14.993 --> 00:03:17.163
I thought you were just
going to go, "Yeah, maybe."

00:03:17.163 --> 00:03:18.497
-Oh, yeah, also, Jimmy,

00:03:18.497 --> 00:03:20.566
I got a Def Jam kids album
coming out this year, too,

00:03:20.566 --> 00:03:22.068
something for the kids,
so, you know,

00:03:22.068 --> 00:03:23.536
we thinking about
those babies, too.

00:03:23.536 --> 00:03:26.706
-That's why I love you, man.

00:03:26.706 --> 00:03:28.541
We talked last time
you were on the show --

00:03:28.541 --> 00:03:31.109
We were saying, "What would you
be if you weren't a rapper?"

00:03:31.109 --> 00:03:33.813
And I was trying to --

00:03:33.813 --> 00:03:35.815
I guessed that you
would be a gamer.

00:03:35.815 --> 00:03:37.951
I thought that might be
what you would be,

00:03:37.951 --> 00:03:41.254
but you said that
you would be a pastor.

00:03:41.254 --> 00:03:42.789
-Yeah.
-Yeah, and --

00:03:42.789 --> 00:03:44.523
[ Laughter ]

00:03:44.523 --> 00:03:46.059
And now here's --

00:03:46.059 --> 00:03:47.827
-Some of the best preachers
come from this --

00:03:47.827 --> 00:03:49.662
from the wrong side
to the right side.

00:03:49.662 --> 00:03:52.531
That's why I say that,
because when you tested,

00:03:52.531 --> 00:03:53.833
you give a testimony,

00:03:53.833 --> 00:03:56.535
and most preachers that are
very good at what they do

00:03:56.535 --> 00:03:57.670
have the best testimonies

00:03:57.670 --> 00:03:59.038
because they've been
through the storm,

00:03:59.038 --> 00:04:00.539
they've been through the worst,

00:04:00.539 --> 00:04:03.309
and they can give you
understanding and explanation

00:04:03.309 --> 00:04:05.644
to what you're going through and
what you're about to go through.

00:04:05.644 --> 00:04:07.980
-Yeah, well,
I totally agree with you.

00:04:07.980 --> 00:04:10.282
That is actually --

00:04:10.282 --> 00:04:11.817
That's correct.

00:04:11.817 --> 00:04:16.789
But in this new show "BMF,"
you actually play a pastor.

00:04:16.789 --> 00:04:18.790
And I was like, "He did it.
He dreamed it."

00:04:18.790 --> 00:04:20.092
-I'm a manifester, Jimmy.

00:04:20.092 --> 00:04:21.994
I'm one of those guys
that they call a manifester,

00:04:21.994 --> 00:04:23.563
so I manifested it.
-Manifester, dude.

00:04:23.563 --> 00:04:26.299
-I spoke on it,
and it came to life.

00:04:26.299 --> 00:04:27.533
-You did.

00:04:27.533 --> 00:04:30.436
What does "BMF" stand for?

00:04:30.436 --> 00:04:32.739
-Black Mafia Family.
-Yeah.

00:04:32.739 --> 00:04:36.876
-That's an organization that was
very, very popular in Atlanta

00:04:36.876 --> 00:04:39.378
in the early 2000s,

00:04:39.378 --> 00:04:41.447
and Detroit is where
they originated.

00:04:41.447 --> 00:04:45.551
There were brothers
who started in the drug trade

00:04:45.551 --> 00:04:48.987
and made it very famous
and launched a lot of careers,

00:04:48.987 --> 00:04:52.825
and they were part of culture,
style, fashion,

00:04:52.825 --> 00:04:55.194
and their story
is damn sure worth seeing.

00:04:55.194 --> 00:04:56.895
It's on the Starz network
on Sunday nights,

00:04:56.895 --> 00:04:57.964
